List every codec the headphones offer; never select a codec this daemon was started without.

Disco runs this aptX BlueALSA with LDAC turned off (--codec=-ldac): LDAC audio through it hung the Disc until the
watchdog rebooted it (Nov 2026), so LDAC always runs on FiiO's own BlueALSA. Two changes make that safe and
still let Disco learn a pair's whole codec list from this daemon:
- GetCodecs ("Available codecs") reports every SEP of the device, not only the codecs enabled here. Upstream hides
  disabled ones, so a daemon started on one codec reported a partial list.
- SelectCodec refuses a codec that is not enabled. Upstream does not check, so a client (the stock player's codec
  request, say) could still switch the link to LDAC.

--- a/src/bluealsa-dbus.c
+++ b/src/bluealsa-dbus.c
@@ -266,10 +266,9 @@
 	if ((codec = a2dp_codec_lookup(sep->codec_id, !sep->dir)) == NULL)
 		return false;
 
-	/* Do not report SEP if corresponding codec is not enabled
-	 * in BlueALSA - it will be not possible to use it. */
-	if (!codec->enabled)
-		return false;
+	/* (diskOS Disco: report every SEP the device has, also for codecs not enabled
+	 * here, so the device's whole codec list is known whatever this daemon was
+	 * started with. A disabled codec still can not be selected: see SelectCodec.) */
 
 	uint8_t caps[sizeof(sep->capabilities)];
 	size_t size = MIN(sep->capabilities_size, sizeof(caps));
@@ -733,6 +732,12 @@
 			goto fail;
 		}
 
+		/* (diskOS Disco: never switch to a codec this daemon was started without.) */
+		if (!codec->enabled) {
+			errmsg = "SEP codec not enabled";
+			goto fail;
+		}
+
 		/* setup default codec configuration */
 		memcpy(&sep->configuration, &sep->capabilities, sep->capabilities_size);
 		if (a2dp_select_configuration(codec, &sep->configuration, sep->capabilities_size) == -1)
